.TH LLITE.OPEN_CACHE_REOPEN_HIST 4 2026-10-02 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
llite.open_cache_reopen_hist \- reopen times of open cache misses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param llite." INSTANCE .open_cache_reopen_hist
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per client mountpoint
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present on client
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR open_cache_reopen_hist (4)
parameter shows how long after the last close of a file
the file was reopened with an open RPC to the MDS,
because the client had no open handle for the file.
It is the distribution of the
.B miss_reopen_time
counter of
.BR llite.open_cache_stats (4),
and can be used to choose a value for
.BR llite.*.opencache_threshold_ms .
The first open of a file on the client has no last close and is not included.
.PP
The histogram has power-of-two buckets.
Each line has the upper limit of the bucket in milliseconds,
the number of missed reopens within that limit and above the previous one,
the percentage of all missed reopens in the bucket,
and the cumulative percentage up to and including the bucket.
Buckets above the longest reopen time are not printed.
.PP
The cumulative percentage is the share of the missed reopens
that are within the given time of the last close, so that setting
.B opencache_threshold_ms
to that time would request an open lock for them,
and later opens of those files could use the cached open handle.
Reopens within the current
.B opencache_threshold_ms
are also in the histogram, since the open that requests the open lock
still needs an open RPC.
.PP
The histogram is reset by writing any value to
.BR llite.*.open_cache_stats .
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B llite.*.open_cache_reopen_hist
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show how long after the last close the missed reopens happened.
Here 90% of the missed reopens were within 16 milliseconds of the last close:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl get_param llite.*.open_cache_reopen_hist"
llite.testfs-ffff888150068000.open_cache_reopen_hist=
snapshot_time:            1790789687.052634017 secs.nsecs
start_time:               1790789686.511679375 secs.nsecs
elapsed_time:             0.540954642 secs.nsecs
reopen_ms           misses    %  cum%
         1:              2   20   20
         2:              0    0   20
         4:              1   10   30
         8:              2   20   50
        16:              4   40   90
        32:              0    0   90
        64:              1   10  100
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llite.*.open_cache_reopen_hist
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_59
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llite.open_cache_stats (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
